※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4503

※ A `comptime foreach` is written out, one body per turn, which is what lets
※ each turn's value be of a different type.  A tuple is the only thing whose
※ values are of types written one by one; everything else holds values of one
※ type, and a loop over one of those is an ordinary loop.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦3⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8⟧
    comptime foreach x := v:
        0u6
    0u6
